# Documentation Guidelines

This is a **pointer**, not the definition. This file used to restate a `/docs` folder structure and
decision checklist for the "SKU Inventory Manager project" — stale in two ways (#365): the product
framing, and a `/docs` layout (`docs/architecture/system-architecture.md`,
`docs/database/schema.md`, `docs/api/specification.md`, `docs/development/`) that's a small, dated
subset of the real tree (which also has `docs/ops/`, `docs/compliance/`, `docs/process/`,
`docs/ai/`, `docs/architecture/adr/`, and more).

**Read `AGENTS.md` in full and follow it**, specifically its "Mandatory Documentation Lookup Order"
and doc-authority rules (`docs/` governed docs ranked by `authority_level` frontmatter —
`authoritative` > `reference` > `historical`). Do not duplicate that content here — a second,
independently-drifting copy of the same doc-hierarchy rule is exactly the staleness failure this
file itself became an example of.
